{"$schema":"https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"artifacts":[{"contents":{"text":"<scxml xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml\" version=\"1.0\" datamodel=\"ecmascript\" initial=\"a\">\n  <datamodel><data id=\"x\" expr=\"0\"/><data id=\"o\" expr=\"({})\"/></datamodel>\n  <state id=\"a\">\n    <transition event=\"e1\" cond=\"x ? 1\" target=\"b\"/>\n    <transition event=\"e2\" cond=\"x + 1 = 2\" target=\"b\"/>\n    <transition event=\"e3\" cond=\"o.a.b = 3\" target=\"b\"/>\n    <transition event=\"e4\" cond=\"x.1\" target=\"b\"/>\n    <transition event=\"e5\" cond=\"let y = 1\" target=\"b\"/>\n    <transition event=\"e6\" cond=\"function() {}\" target=\"b\"/>\n    <transition event=\"e7\" cond=\"x in\" target=\"b\"/>\n    <transition event=\"e8\" cond=\"'unterminated\" target=\"b\"/>\n  </state>\n  <final id=\"b\"/>\n</scxml>\n"},"location":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"mimeType":"application/scxml+xml"}],"columnKind":"utf16CodeUnits","properties":{"diagnosticCounts":{"errors":0,"notes":0,"total":7,"warnings":7},"producer":{"kind":"validator"}},"results":[{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":39,"endLine":4,"startColumn":38,"startLine":4}}}],"message":{"markdown":"ecmascript syntax error in `cond`: the expression ends before it is complete\n\n**Note:** a condition that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` and evaluates as false, so this condition can never hold\n\n**Help:** a `?` conditional needs both branches: `test ? whenTrue : whenFalse`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"ecmascript syntax error in `cond`: the expression ends before it is complete"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":227,"start":226},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"while parsing this `cond`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":39,"endLine":4,"startColumn":34,"startLine":4}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML038"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":1,"byteOffset":281,"endColumn":41,"endLine":5,"startColumn":40,"startLine":5},"insertedContent":{"text":"==="}}]}],"description":{"text":"compare with `===`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":41,"endLine":5,"startColumn":40,"startLine":5}}}],"message":{"markdown":"ecmascript syntax error in `cond`: the left side of `=` cannot be assigned to\n\n**Note:** a condition that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` and evaluates as false, so this condition can never hold\n\n**Help:** `=` assigns, and only a variable or a property such as `a.b` or `a[0]` can be assigned; to compare, write `===` (or `==`)\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"ecmascript syntax error in `cond`: the left side of `=` cannot be assigned to"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":282,"start":281},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"while parsing this `cond`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":43,"endLine":5,"startColumn":34,"startLine":5}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML038"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":1,"byteOffset":338,"endColumn":41,"endLine":6,"startColumn":40,"startLine":6},"insertedContent":{"text":"==="}}]}],"description":{"text":"compare with `===`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":41,"endLine":6,"startColumn":40,"startLine":6}}}],"message":{"markdown":"`cond` on `<transition>` has a side effect\n\n**Note:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9.1: \"Conditional expressions in conformant SCXML documents SHOULD NOT have side effects.\" (Appendix B's \"This language MUST not have side effects\" contradicts official IRP test 444, `cond=\"++var1==2\"`; see docs/spec-errata.md)\n\n**Help:** to compare, use `===` (or `==`); to change the value, move the assignment into `<assign>` in the transition\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 Appendix B Data Models\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9.1 Conditional Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"`cond` on `<transition>` has a side effect"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":339,"start":338},"category":"lint"},"ruleId":"SCXML076"},{"fixes":[{"artifactChanges":[{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"replacements":[{"deletedRegion":{"byteLength":2,"byteOffset":390,"endColumn":37,"endLine":7,"startColumn":35,"startLine":7},"insertedContent":{"text":"[1]"}}]}],"description":{"text":"index with `[1]`"},"properties":{"applicability":"maybe-incorrect"}}],"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":37,"endLine":7,"startColumn":35,"startLine":7}}}],"message":{"markdown":"ecmascript syntax error in `cond`: `.1` is not a property access\n\n**Note:** a condition that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` and evaluates as false, so this condition can never hold\n\n**Help:** a property name cannot start with a digit; index with brackets: `[1]`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"ecmascript syntax error in `cond`: `.1` is not a property access"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":392,"start":390},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"while parsing this `cond`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":37,"endLine":7,"startColumn":34,"startLine":7}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML038"},{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":37,"endLine":8,"startColumn":34,"startLine":8}}}],"message":{"markdown":"ecmascript syntax error in `cond`: `let` declares a variable, which a `cond` cannot do\n\n**Note:** a condition that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` and evaluates as false, so this condition can never hold\n\n**Help:** a `cond` must be an expression: declare the variable with `<data id=\"y\" expr=\"…\"/>` in the `<datamodel>`, or set it with `<assign location=\"y\" expr=\"…\"/>`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"ecmascript syntax error in `cond`: `let` declares a variable, which a `cond` cannot do"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":443,"start":440},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"while parsing this `cond`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":43,"endLine":8,"startColumn":34,"startLine":8}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML038"},{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":38,"endLine":10,"startColumn":37,"startLine":10}}}],"message":{"markdown":"ecmascript syntax error in `cond`: the expression ends before it is complete\n\n**Note:** a condition that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` and evaluates as false, so this condition can never hold\n\n**Help:** add the missing operand, closing bracket, or closing quote at the end\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"ecmascript syntax error in `cond`: the expression ends before it is complete"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":562,"start":561},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"while parsing this `cond`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":38,"endLine":10,"startColumn":34,"startLine":10}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML038"},{"level":"warning","locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":35,"endLine":11,"startColumn":34,"startLine":11}}}],"message":{"markdown":"ecmascript syntax error in `cond`: unterminated string literal\n\n**Note:** a condition that cannot be parsed raises `error.execution` and evaluates as false, so this condition can never hold\n\n**Help:** close the string with a matching `'`; to include a `'` inside it, escape it as `\\'`\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §5.9 Expressions\n\n**Spec:** SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model","text":"ecmascript syntax error in `cond`: unterminated string literal"},"properties":{"byteSpan":{"end":611,"start":610},"category":"lint"},"relatedLocations":[{"id":1,"message":{"text":"while parsing this `cond`"},"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"tests/ui/scxml038-ecmascript-parse-paths.scx"},"region":{"endColumn":47,"endLine":11,"startColumn":34,"startLine":11}}}],"ruleId":"SCXML038"}],"tool":{"driver":{"informationUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/","name":"scxml-validator","rules":[{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML 1.0 §5.9.4: \"The SCXML Processor MAY reject documents containing syntactically ill-formed expressions at document load time, or it MAY wait and place 'error.execution' in the internal event queue at runtime when the expressions are evaluated.\" This toolchain takes the second option, so the document compiles and the expression raises `error.execution` whenever it is evaluated (a condition is then false and the rest of an executable-content block is skipped); this check runs only when the host supplies the data model's parse-only syntax capability (the native CLI links the ECMAScript and XPath checkers). Each finding names the offending source text and, where a repair is certain to parse, offers it: ECMAScript habits in XPath (`==` to `=`, `&&` to `and`, `||` to `or`, `!x` to `not(x)`, `length()` to `string-length()`), a stray `=` in ECMAScript (`x === = 3`), word operators, quoting, and more. The XPath data model has no script language, so a non-empty `<script>` is reported too"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: apply the suggested repair, or fix the syntax at the marked position following the finding's help; for XPath, use XPath 1.0 operators and functions (`=`, `and`, `or`, `not()`, `string-length()`, `count()`).\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §B.2 The ECMAScript Data Model\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML038` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#ecma-profile","id":"SCXML038","name":"SCXML038","properties":{"category":"semantic"},"shortDescription":{"text":"an expression or script does not parse in the selected data model"}},{"defaultConfiguration":{"level":"warning"},"fullDescription":{"text":"SCXML 1.0 §5.9.1: \"Conditional expressions in conformant SCXML documents SHOULD NOT have side effects.\" Appendix B also says a data model's condition language \"MUST not have side effects\", but official W3C IRP test 444 requires `cond=\"++var1==2\"` to run and increment `var1`, so the processor follows the IRP (docs/spec-errata.md) and a certain side effect in an ECMAScript condition (an assignment, update, or `delete` outside the condition, a mutating built-in, `Math.random`, or a call of a document function that does one of those) is a warning, not an error"},"help":{"text":"How to fix: compute the condition without changing anything, and move the change into the transition's executable content (`<assign>` or `<script>`); to compare, use `===`.\n\nSpecification: SCXML 1.0 §5.9.1 Conditional Expressions\n\nRun `scx --explain SCXML076` for examples."},"helpUri":"https://www.w3.org/TR/scxml/#ConditionalExpressions","id":"SCXML076","name":"SCXML076","properties":{"category":"lint"},"shortDescription":{"text":"a condition has a side effect"}}],"semanticVersion":"0.2.0"}}}],"version":"2.1.0"}